# Nero Quest pose frame correction and simulation retest

- Date: 2026-09-29 (Asia/Shanghai)
- Deployment: `/home/loopkok/NEXUS` on `192.168.0.231`
- Profile: `nero_dual_xhand_mujoco`
- Profile SHA256: `bc7b5a34cd066f9bdffa06cce939ef681f10149314691f50b1fe3437ac78d3fc`
- ROS isolation: `ROS_DOMAIN_ID=89`, `ROS_LOCALHOST_ONLY=1`
- Hardware boundary: simulation only. No CAN, real robot driver, Quest receiver, physical
  camera, or hand hardware was started.

## Corrected frame path

1. Quest wrist/controller poses use the XNero left/right rotation selected by the Nero
   assembly profile. The Quest ROS adapter applies that mapping once and bypasses the
   generic `convert_to_robot` conversion for these wrist poses.
2. Hand landmarks and body/head data retain their existing generic conversion setting.
3. NEXUS Nero profiles use identity `vr_to_arm_rot`. Nero teleop anchors to measured
   `link7` FK and passes the Quest flange target directly to the unchanged Nero IK solver.
4. `frame_transforms.link7_to_xhand_palm` contains physical palm geometry for FK/model
   parity only; it is not part of the teleop target path.

## Verification

- Remote build: `quest3_hand_mocap`, `nexus_core`, and `nero_mujoco_sim` passed.
- Remote tests on the deployed build: NEXUS contract 16/16, Quest basis mapping 3/3,
  Nero MuJoCo 6/6. The final local revision adds explicit `per_side` override tests;
  the local Quest pose-mapping suite passes 6/6.
- ROS synthetic-input acceptance: PASS. Each of the four final command topics had one
  publisher. Joint state, commands, Quest wrist/hand/Joy bridge, and three synthetic
  compressed camera streams flowed through the isolated simulation graph.
- For a synthetic Quest input of 8 mm amplitude and `motion_scale=0.65`, desired link7
  X peak-to-peak was 10.4 mm. MuJoCo measured 9.835 mm left and 9.856 mm right
  (94.6% and 94.8%); input/tracking correlation was 0.964 and 0.962. Maximum link7
  orientation drift was 0.0354 degrees on each side. IK candidate FK moved 10.36 mm in X;
  off-axis Y/Z excursion remained below 1.1 mm in measured physics state.
- Input-to-candidate latency: left p50/p95/max 1.84/21.12/34.77 ms; right
  8.53/11.82/57.11 ms. Wrist loss paused arbitration after 845 ms, with zero wrist
  messages received after publisher shutdown.
- MuJoCo FK parity tests still pass for link7 and the independent physical XHand palm frame.

## Data/model scope

The recorder returned to IDLE and accumulated a 2.38 MB session, but no complete episode was
reported (`episode_counts={}`, `episode_index=-1`). This run therefore does not establish
quality/export for the corrected profile hash. The earlier 442-frame quality/export run and
ACT model used the previous profile SHA256 `046547d23b5effc16707016208fe5a11f44641f80064df2f744c01b9f9a84167`;
they remain historical results and must be regenerated/retrained before claiming current
profile data or checkpoint compatibility. The profile manifest gate should reject that old
checkpoint under the new hash.

Raw remote evidence is mirrored in:

- `remote-host/test_logs/nero_frame_acceptance_record.json`
- `remote-host/test_logs/nero_frame_system.log`

The deployment host stopped responding to ICMP and SSH after the simulation finished.
The final local-only test/helper refinement and this correction summary could not be
copied back to the host during this session. The remote tested implementation already
uses the same per-side override directly; the final local helper makes that mode
selection explicit and adds a regression test for bypassing the generic conversion.
